-----------------------
CUMULATIVE FES PLOTTING
-----------------------
Plots cumulative 1D Free Energy Surfaces over time to check the convergence of the simulation.
Calculates histograms using PLUMED native units (kJ/mol and nm) and converts them to kcal/mol and Å for plotting.

## REQUIRED FILES:
Link the following file in the directory:

        - colvar file with weights from step 2 (e.g., COLVAR_WEIGHTED)

## CUMULATIVE FES

module load python

python plot_cumulative_fes.py -f COLVAR_WEIGHTED --cv armsdC --min 0.0 --max 1.5 --bins 100 --nm-to-a

Additional useful flags:
        --wcol      --> specify the weight column (default is "weight", use "weight_walls" if needed)
        --eq-time   --> time to discard as equilibration in ps (default: 400000)
        --step-time --> time step for cumulative blocks in ps (default: 200000)
        -o          --> specify output name (default: cumulative_fes_<cv>.png)

## OUTPUT

A new image file:

        - cumulative_fes_<cv>.png --> A plot showing the FES profile at different time slices.
